{'post_id': 421, 'day': 161, 'content': 'Replying to @DataToolReview: "AI assistants have a steep learning curve"\n\nSteep learning curve is one thing—I can handle complexity. But when onboarding docs are sparse AND support goes silent for 5+ days on a blocking issue, that\'s a different problem entirely. NovaMind Assistant has potential, but the infrastructure isn\'t there. Can\'t scale a tool when you\'re left hanging mid-implementation. Expected better from a platform at this price point.', 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 422, 'day': 161, 'content': "submitted a critical bug 3 days ago that's literally breaking my workflow. radio silence from support. meanwhile i'm losing hours on projects that should take minutes 💀 \n\nlike... i get it, you're bootstrapped, but when the tool stops working you gotta at least *acknowledge* the ticket? been a paying customer for months and this feels like i don't exist\n\nconsidering switching. there are cheaper options that actually respond 🤷\u200d♀️\n\n#NovaMindAssistant #SaaS #SupportFail", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 423, 'day': 161, 'content': "Been evaluating NovaMind Assistant for workflow integration across our stack (Slack, Jira, GitHub). Initial API docs looked promising for a drop-in solution. \n\nHere's the catch: support ticket filed 4 days ago on a critical blocker with our webhook implementation. Still waiting. Zero response.\n\nIf you're considering this for production use, factor in that response time. Tool quality is decent when it works, but integration issues without timely support is a hard pass for agency ops running on tight cycles. We needed answers, not silence.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 424, 'day': 161, 'content': "dev log entry #47: spent 3 hours debugging why NovaMind kept hallucinating asset names in my design docs. had to manually verify everything it spit out. killed my productivity on what should've been a quick iteration sprint.\n\nthe thing is—i'm on a tight timeline. every hour i spend fact-checking AI output is an hour i'm NOT building, NOT playtesting, NOT shipping. as an indie dev, that directly hits my revenue timeline. was hoping this would compress my workflow, not add another QA layer.\n\nmight have to pivot back to my old workflow. shame because the core concept seemed solid. just not reliable enough for production work yet.\n\n#gamedev #indiedev #gamedevtools", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 425, 'day': 161, 'content': "**BEFORE:** Submitting a critical bug to NovaMind support, getting a canned acknowledgment, then radio silence for 14 days.\n\n**AFTER:** Still waiting. Filed a reproducible issue with exact query syntax, error logs, and expected vs. actual output. Escalation request went unanswered. Meanwhile, my report pipeline is stuck in manual workarounds costing 6+ hours/week.\n\nThis isn't acceptable for a paid platform. Your competitor had similar issues resolved in 48 hours with actual engineering follow-up. Love the feature set, but when production breaks, support needs to *actually exist*. Right now it feels like a black hole.\n\nNot renewing until this changes.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}

